1
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:05,830
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:09,500
Ugly Naked Guy is decorating his tree.

3
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:13,000
Oh, my God, you should see the size of his Christmas balls!

4
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:17,470
- Hey.     - Hey.

5
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,340
How much did you tip the super?

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,880
Yeah, we were gonna give 50, but we don't wanna look bad.

7
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,230
Oh, this year we just made him cookies.

8
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:27,600
And 25 it is.

9
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,650
Heh. You gave him cookies?

10
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:32,740
- Money is so impersonal.     - Yeah.

11
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,700
Cookies says someone really cares.

12
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,740
All right, we're broke, but cookies do say that.

13
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:40,990
I can see that.

14
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,290
A plate of brownies told me a limerick.

15
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:50,040
Pheebs, let me ask you something. Were these, uh, "funny" brownies?

16
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,500
Not especially.

17
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:55,170
But, you know, I think they had pot in them.

18
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:00,760
So, you guys, who else did you tip with cookies?

19
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:03,180
Uh, the mailman, the super...

20
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:07,190
Oh, and the newspaper delivery guy.

21
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,520
Oh, my God.

22
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:11,110
What?

23
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:13,070
Uh, I don't think you're gonna like this.

24
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:14,320
Oh, wow.

25
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:16,360
Oh, gosh.

26
00:01:16,530 --> 00:01:19,820
Oh, these are cookies smashed in the Sports section.

27
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:21,950
And he did my crossword puzzle.

28
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,910
Yeah, but not very well, unless 14 across, "Gershwin musical"...

29
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,250
actually is "Bite me, bite me, bite me."

30
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:40,420
∮ So no one told you life was gonna be this way ∮

31
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:45,130
∮ Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. ∮

32
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:49,850
∮ It's like you're always stuck in second gear ∮

33
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:52,410
∮ When it hasn't been your day, ∮

34
00:01:52,410 --> 00:01:55,410
∮ your week, your month, or even your year ∮

35
00:01:55,410 --> 00:01:59,370
∮ but I'll be there for you ∮

36
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:01,200
∮ When the rain starts to pour ∮

37
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,320
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

38
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:06,160
∮ Like I've been there before ∮

39
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:09,170
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

40
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:12,830
∮ 'Cause you're there for me too ∮

41
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:23,180
I can't believe it's Christmas already. You know?

42
00:02:23,350 --> 00:02:26,140
One day you're eating turkey, the next thing you know...

43
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:29,310
your lords are a-leaping and your geese are a-laying. Heh.

44
00:02:30,770 --> 00:02:34,940
Which is why geese are so relaxed this time of year.

45
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,610
- Hey, guys.     - Hey.

46
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:40,990
Hey, Rach.

47
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:44,070
I, uh, got you a little present.

48
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,950
I'll open it.

49
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,410
It's a Slinky!

50
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,710
Ha, ha. Remember, huh?

51
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:55,090
Walks downstairs Alone or in pairs

52
00:02:55,250 --> 00:02:57,130
Everyone knows it's...

53
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,130
Just a big spring.

54
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:03,930
You're still mad because of the whole...

55
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:06,510
Horrible list of reasons not to be with me?

56
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,350
How about we just call it "the unfortunate incident"?

57
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,730
Hey, Gunther. You got stairs in your place?

58
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:18,190
- Yeah.     - Go nuts.

59
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,700
- Hey, guys.     - Hey.

60
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:24,110
What's in the bag?

61
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,490
Mm, just some presents.

62
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:28,700
Come on, show us what you bought.

63
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,830
You know you want to.

64
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:33,710
Okay.

65
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:39,500
This is a picture frame from Ben to my parents.

66
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:41,260
Oh, that's cute.

67
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:44,470
Some "Hers" and "Hers" towels for Susan and Carol.

68
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,970
And, uh, I got this blouse for Mom.

69
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:53,230
- Ross, that is gorgeous!     - Yeah?

70
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:56,060
Look at these authentic fake medals!

71
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:58,070
Mom's gonna be voted "best dressed"...

72
00:03:58,230 --> 00:04:00,360
at the make-believe military academy!

73
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:04,660
- Hey.     - Hey.

74
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:07,950
- Happy Christmas Eve Eve.     - You too.

75
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:10,200
Oh, my God! Where did you get this?

76
00:04:10,370 --> 00:04:13,080
Uh, Macy's, third floor, home furnishings.

77
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:14,580
This is my father!

78
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,420
This is a picture of my dad!

79
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,550
Uh, Pheebs, that's the guy that comes in the frame.

80
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,970
No, it's my dad. I'll show you.

81
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,390
I thought your dad was in prison.

82
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,180
No, that's my stepdad.

83
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:32,720
My real dad's the one that ran out on us before I was born.

84
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,890
How have you never been on Oprah?

85
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:38,810
Look, see? This is him.

86
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:42,650
My mother gave me this picture before she died. Same guy!

87
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:48,370
Honey, uh, this is a picture of the frame guy...

88
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:51,240
posing in front of a blue screen with a collie.

89
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:54,660
It's not a blue screen. It's just...

90
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:57,670
Maybe it was just really clear that day.

91
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:03,090
Okay, I have to talk to my grandmother.

92
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:06,300
- Wait a minute, honey!     - Pheebs.

93
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,010
- Whoa.     - Wow.

94
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:13,060
I'm trying to get my boss's ex-wife to sleep with me.

95
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:15,270
Joey.

96
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:18,690
Oh, but when Phoebe has a problem, everyone's all ears!

97
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,940
Esther Livingston.

98
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:26,990
Gone!

99
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,700
Um... Hi, Pooh.

100
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:33,160
Hi, Gram. Ahem, what you doing?

101
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:35,870
Oh, just updating the phone book.

102
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:39,330
Um, Gram? Um...

103
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,750
Can I see the pictures of my dad again?

104
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,750
Oh.

105
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,010
Oh, sure, sure.

106
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:47,630
Uh... Huh, how come?

107
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,470
Just, you know, to see him.

108
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,640
Oh, sure. Here.

109
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:54,060
All right, uh...

110
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:57,230
This is the one of your father in a meadow.

111
00:05:58,190 --> 00:06:01,810
And, uh, helping a little boy fly a kite.

112
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:05,440
And here he is at a graduation.

113
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,200
Another graduation.

114
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,700
Another graduation.

115
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:16,750
Is this really my father?

116
00:06:17,290 --> 00:06:18,910
Is it really your...?

117
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:22,540
Well, of course it is.

118
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:26,710
I smell smoke. Maybe because someone's pants are on fire!

119
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,840
Well, I...

120
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:31,890
In all the years we've been grandmother and granddaughter...

121
00:06:32,050 --> 00:06:33,600
you've never lied.

122
00:06:35,010 --> 00:06:39,270
All right, that's not your father. It's a picture of a guy in a frame.

123
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,650
Oh, God.

124
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,650
It was your mother's idea.

125
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,240
She didn't want you to know your real father...

126
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:50,360
because it hurt her so much when he left.

127
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:52,570
I didn't wanna go along with it.

128
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:56,120
But then she died and it was harder to argue with her.

129
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,080
Not impossible, but harder.

130
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:04,880
All right. So he's not a famous tree surgeon?

131
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:13,640
And I guess he doesn't live in a hut in Burma where there's no phones?

132
00:07:14,430 --> 00:07:17,510
Last I heard, he was a pharmacist somewhere upstate.

133
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,310
That makes no sense.

134
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,640
Why would the villagers worship a pharmacist?

135
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,270
Honey.

136
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,610
- Oh. Yeah.     - Yeah.

137
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:32,820
Anyway, that's all I know.

138
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:36,450
That...

139
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,950
and this.

140
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,040
This...

141
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,920
is the real him.

142
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:50,210
Oh.

143
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:55,050
I remember my father all dressed up in the red suit...

144
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:58,390
the big black boots and the patent leather belt...

145
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,640
sneaking around downstairs. He didn't want us to see him...

146
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:06,520
but he'd be drunk, so he'd crash into something and wake everybody up.

147
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:09,860
That doesn't sound like a very merry Christmas.

148
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:12,240
Who said anything about Christmas?

149
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:17,870
- Hi.     - Anyone hear from Phoebe yet?

150
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,410
No, nothing.

151
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:20,990
I hope she's okay.

152
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,160
I know exactly what she's going through.

153
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:25,710
How do you know what she's going through?

154
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,460
She told us.

155
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,590
What do you got there, Monica?

156
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,050
Stuff for the party.

157
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:37,140
Aren't you guys supposed to be shopping?

158
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,970
You didn't buy presents yet?

159
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:41,850
Tomorrow's Christmas Eve! What are you gonna do?

160
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:45,020
Don't you have to be Claymation to say stuff like that?

161
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:49,860
Oh, by the way, Mon, I don't think the mailman liked your cookies.

162
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:51,900
Here are the ornaments your mom sent.

163
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:56,240
Well...

164
00:08:56,450 --> 00:09:00,580
Maybe the mailman liked the cookies. We just didn't give him enough.

165
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:03,790
Monica, pigeons learn faster than you.

166
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,090
Hey, Rach. Ahem.

167
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:16,220
I think I know what will make you feel better.

168
00:09:16,430 --> 00:09:19,220
How about you make a list about me?

169
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:21,600
Forget it. I'm not gonna stand here...

170
00:09:21,810 --> 00:09:22,970
and make a list.

171
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:25,140
Okay, you're whiny...

172
00:09:25,350 --> 00:09:28,270
you are obsessive, you are insecure...

173
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,190
- you're gutless.     - Heh.

174
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,440
You don't ever just seize the day.

175
00:09:32,690 --> 00:09:35,650
You liked me for a year and you didn't do anything about it.

176
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:39,070
And, uh... Oh, you wear too much of that gel in your hair.

177
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,410
See, there. You, uh...

178
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:47,160
All right, you did what I said.

179
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:49,620
- And you know what?     - Hmm?

180
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:51,590
You're right. I do feel better.

181
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:52,840
Thank you, Ross.

182
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:03,430
Yeah, in Albany. Could I have the number of Frank Buffay?

183
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:07,560
Okay. Um, in lthaca?

184
00:10:08,390 --> 00:10:10,900
All right, um, Saratoga?

185
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,400
Oneonta?

186
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:17,360
You know what? You shouldn't call yourself Information!

187
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:23,490
Hey.

188
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:27,540
Hello, Grandma. If that is, in fact, your real name.

189
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,920
Come on now, Pooh. Don't still be mad at me.

190
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:35,380
- How's it going?     - Oh, not so good.

191
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:39,920
Upstate's pretty big. He's pretty small. You do the math.

192
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,600
Well, I think you're better off without him.

193
00:10:44,430 --> 00:10:46,560
Oh, honey, I know he's your daddy.

194
00:10:46,770 --> 00:10:49,930
But to me, he's still the irresponsible creep...

195
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:54,190
who locked up your mom and stole her Gremlin.

196
00:10:55,230 --> 00:10:59,360
I know. I just wanted to know who he was, you know?

197
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,450
Yeah, I know.

198
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:05,200
Okay.

199
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:09,700
I wasn't completely honest with you when I told you that, uh, I didn't know...

200
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:12,170
exactly where he lived.

201
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,130
What do you mean?

202
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:18,380
He lives at 74 Laurel Drive in Middletown.

203
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:23,260
If you hit the Dairy Queen, you've gone too far.

204
00:11:23,470 --> 00:11:25,300
You can take my cab.

205
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:26,850
Wow.

206
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,310
Thank you.

207
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:33,310
- Nobody else drives that cab.     - Uh-huh. Got it.

208
00:11:33,650 --> 00:11:34,730
Oh.

209
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:37,230
- I'm gonna see my dad!     - Ha-ha-ha.

210
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:40,240
- Thank you.     - Oh. Ha, ha.

211
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,860
Mm, okay. Oh.

212
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:44,360
Wish me luck, Grandpa.

213
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:53,830
Hey.

214
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,420
Phoebe here with the cab yet?

215
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:58,250
Yeah, she brought the invisible cab.

216
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,750
Hop in!

217
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:03,170
She'd better get here. The stores close at 7.

218
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:06,220
It'll be two hours to Phoebe's dad's house...

219
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:08,510
they'll meet, chat, swap life stories.

220
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:10,350
We'll still have plenty of time.

221
00:12:11,810 --> 00:12:13,730
- Hey, here she comes!     - Hey.

222
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:16,060
Hey, hey.

223
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,060
Hi.

224
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,690
- Hey.     - Hey.

225
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,450
Can you believe this?

226
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:25,950
In like two hours I'm gonna have a dad.

227
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:29,240
Yeah, big stuff.

228
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:30,870
- Okay, let's go.     - Okay.

229
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:33,040
- Here, you have to hold this.     - Okay.

230
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,500
"Brake, left. Gas, right"?

231
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:40,710
Uh-huh, that's my cheat sheet.

232
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:47,300
- Where's my seat belt?     - That side doesn't have one.

233
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:50,180
The paramedics had to cut through it.

234
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,190
- Hey.     - Hey.

235
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:03,780
Come on, just tell me. Please, please.

236
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:09,200
For the 16th time, no, I do not think you're obsessive.

237
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,580
- Oh, it's hot in here!     - Rach, get the heat.

238
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:16,500
- Ross, turn the heat down, please?     - Sure.

239
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,830
There's a difference between obsessive...

240
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,170
Ross, the heat!

241
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:24,460
Okay. Heat, heat, heat. And I'm the obsessive one?

242
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,420
Okay.

243
00:13:26,590 --> 00:13:28,340
This way is on.

244
00:13:28,590 --> 00:13:31,470
So this is...

245
00:13:33,470 --> 00:13:35,100
off.

246
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:38,350
Did you just break the radiator?

247
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:41,480
No, I was turning the knob and...

248
00:13:41,730 --> 00:13:43,440
here it is.

249
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:44,860
Well, put it back!

250
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:48,950
It, uh...

251
00:13:49,110 --> 00:13:52,160
- It won't go back.     - Ugh. I'll call the super.

252
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:53,790
Here, let me try.

253
00:13:53,950 --> 00:13:58,160
Oh, oh, that's right. I forgot about your ability to fuse metal.

254
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,120
Hey, it's Funny's cousin...

255
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:01,420
Not Funny!

256
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,250
Hi, Mr. Treeger?

257
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:05,380
It's Rachel Green from upstairs.

258
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:08,630
Yes, somebody, uh, broke our knob on the radiator...

259
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:11,680
and it's really hot in here.

260
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:14,850
Yes, it's hot enough to bake cookies.

261
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:19,980
Well, do you think we could have a new one by 6?

262
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,980
What? No, no. Tuesday? We can't wait until Tuesday.

263
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:24,940
We're having a party tonight.

264
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:26,440
Okay, tip the man.

265
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:28,530
If he doesn't like our cookies, too bad.

266
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:30,490
I won't be blackmailed.

267
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,950
Look, if it gets a little warm...

268
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,830
it can be a theme party.

269
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,830
Here's a theme: "Come on in, live like bacon!"

270
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,330
Ooh, this is it.

271
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:44,250
Seventy-four.

272
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:48,260
Oh, so that's what this is for!

273
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,550
Wow.

274
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:52,680
This is it. I'm gonna meet my dad.

275
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,010
This is, like, the biggest thing ever, huh?

276
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:57,270
- Yeah.     - Sure is.

277
00:14:57,470 --> 00:14:59,140
Here I go. I'm going in.

278
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:00,390
All right!

279
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,850
Good luck, Pheebs.

280
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:03,610
Okay.

281
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:05,670
Here I go.

282
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:09,140
Here I go.

283
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:12,240
I'm going.

284
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:25,380
Hi.

285
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:27,960
Welcome to our tropical Christmas party, heh.

286
00:15:28,130 --> 00:15:31,720
Put your coats, sweaters, pants and shirts in the bedroom.

287
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:36,600
It's hard to tell because I'm sweating...

288
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,850
but I use exactly what the gel bottle says.

289
00:15:42,350 --> 00:15:46,770
An amount about the size of a pea. How can that be too much?

290
00:15:49,530 --> 00:15:51,110
Ice?

291
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:54,910
Ice? Ice squares anyone? Take a napkin.

292
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:56,160
All right.

293
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:58,240
Monica. Monica!

294
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:02,410
Monica, your guests are turning into jerky.

295
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:04,750
Really? I'm perfectly comfortable.

296
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:08,000
Ha, ha. Hey! Get in line, buddy. I was next.

297
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,970
Mr. Treeger.

298
00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:15,550
You said there was a party.

299
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,050
Oh, yeah.

300
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:18,810
Well, hey, welcome to our sauna.

301
00:16:18,970 --> 00:16:22,850
Uh, is it hot? My body always stays cool.

302
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:25,480
Probably because I have so much skin.

303
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,190
Hey, cheese!

304
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:32,610
Here's the chance. Monica, give him cash.

305
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:35,950
Rachel, give him your earrings. Something. Anything!

306
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,700
No, I will not cave.

307
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:38,950
I'm with Mon.

308
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:42,410
All right. You know how you say I never seize the day?

309
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:46,000
Even though he's your super, I'm seizing.

310
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:48,920
Mr. Treeger?

311
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,960
Here is 50 bucks. Merry Christmas.

312
00:16:53,170 --> 00:16:54,380
Oh, wow.

313
00:16:54,550 --> 00:16:55,630
I didn't get you anything.

314
00:16:57,010 --> 00:16:59,010
Here's five back.

315
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:02,560
No, that's your Christmas tip.

316
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:07,270
Oh, do you think there's a chance you can fix that radiator now?

317
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:09,730
No can do. Like I told the girl...

318
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,730
I can't get a knob until Tuesday.

319
00:17:12,530 --> 00:17:14,150
- Ross?     - Yeah?

320
00:17:14,320 --> 00:17:16,070
He's playing baseball.

321
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,070
You mean hardball?

322
00:17:21,410 --> 00:17:22,490
Whatever.

323
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:24,330
What you gonna do?

324
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,660
Excuse me. I'm seizing.

325
00:17:26,870 --> 00:17:28,880
Mr. Treeger?

326
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,210
Here's another 50.

327
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:33,050
Happy Hanukkah.

328
00:17:33,210 --> 00:17:36,340
Will, uh, this help with the knob-getting?

329
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:37,760
No.

330
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:40,890
The place is not open till Tuesday.

331
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,430
Am I not saying it right?

332
00:17:44,810 --> 00:17:47,100
So you really did like my cookies?

333
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:51,110
Oh, yeah, they were so personal. It really showed you cared.

334
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,320
Nice seizing...

335
00:17:58,530 --> 00:18:00,410
gel boy.

336
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,620
So, uh...

337
00:18:04,830 --> 00:18:06,750
Is this, uh, mistletoe?

338
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,420
No, uh, that...

339
00:18:10,670 --> 00:18:12,880
That is basil.

340
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:16,050
- Oh.     - Yeah.

341
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:19,220
If it was mistletoe, I was gonna kiss you.

342
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:23,180
No, it's still basil.

343
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,070
Okay.

344
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:40,860
- How far did you get?     - Mailbox.

345
00:18:41,070 --> 00:18:44,080
- All right, we're getting closer.     - Uh-huh.

346
00:18:45,490 --> 00:18:46,660
What's going on?

347
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:50,290
It's just, like, a whole mess of stuff.

348
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:55,040
Like yesterday, my dad was this famous Burma tree-surgeon guy.

349
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:58,710
And, you know, now he's, uh, a pharmacist guy and...

350
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:03,050
Well, maybe he's this really cool pharmacist guy.

351
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:07,640
Yeah, maybe. And I'll knock on the door...

352
00:19:07,810 --> 00:19:11,060
and he'll hug me, and I'll have a dad.

353
00:19:11,270 --> 00:19:14,900
I'll go to his pharmacy and everyone will be nice to me...

354
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:18,070
because, you know, I'm Frank's daughter.

355
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:19,610
So why not go knock?

356
00:19:23,410 --> 00:19:28,490
Because, I mean, what if he's not this great dad guy?

357
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:33,750
What if he's still the dirtbag who ran out on my mom and us?

358
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,500
- Yeah.     - Hmm.

359
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:40,050
You know what?

360
00:19:40,670 --> 00:19:43,680
I've already lost a fake dad this week.

361
00:19:44,890 --> 00:19:47,760
I don't think I'm ready to lose a real one.

362
00:19:49,850 --> 00:19:53,560
Pheebs, that's okay. You took a big step today.

363
00:19:54,650 --> 00:19:56,310
- Yeah?     - Yeah.

364
00:19:56,480 --> 00:20:00,030
Someday, when you're ready, you'll make it past the hedges.

365
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:03,070
And when you do, he'll be lucky to have you.

366
00:20:04,110 --> 00:20:05,820
You guys.

367
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:11,330
Sorry about your shopping.

368
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:14,960
Oh, that's okay. We'll figure something out.

369
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:19,380
I know you're not going in there...

370
00:20:19,590 --> 00:20:23,090
but do you think it'd be all right if I went in and used his bathroom?

371
00:20:24,050 --> 00:20:26,510
That's fine, never mind.

372
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:29,220
Cool, snow!

373
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:31,930
Kind of like a blank canvas.

374
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:44,530
Ho-ho-ho-holy crap, is it hot in here!

375
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:49,030
You mind if I turn the heat down?

376
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:52,620
We could have used that kind of thinking earlier!

377
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:54,660
So, Pheebs, how did it go?

378
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:56,920
Oh, ahem, I couldn't go in.

379
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,250
- Honey, I'm sorry.     - Are you okay?

380
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:02,260
Yeah, it's okay, because I know he's there.

381
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:04,340
So that's enough for now.

382
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:07,720
Hey, it's after midnight! Merry Christmas, everyone!

383
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:11,560
Oh, right! Merry Christmas!

384
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:14,310
The knob was broken...

385
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:18,150
so I turned it off from underneath. I hope that's all right.

386
00:21:30,410 --> 00:21:32,490
Rach, these are for you.

387
00:21:33,410 --> 00:21:35,540
Wiper blades.

388
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:37,500
I don't even have a car.

389
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:41,790
Ha, ha. No, but with this new-car smell, you'll think you do.

390
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:47,300
Okay, Pheebs, your turn.

391
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,510
Toilet-seat covers.

392
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:57,690
Is that what you were doing while I was getting gas?

393
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:59,020
- Uh-huh.     - Mm-hm.

394
00:21:59,190 --> 00:22:01,190
You guys!

395
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,610
And for Ross...

396
00:22:02,770 --> 00:22:05,190
Mr. Sweet Tooth.

397
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,240
You got me a cola drink?

398
00:22:10,450 --> 00:22:13,200
And a lemon-lime!

399
00:22:15,450 --> 00:22:20,120
Well, this is too much. I feel like I should get you another sweater.

400
00:22:22,290 --> 00:22:24,880
And last but not least...

401
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:29,590
They're ribbed for your pleasure.

